	I got a hold of my DEC Support before I could get any replies back from 
you folks.  Anyway, I wanted to tell you what he told me.
	
Basically I had to edit the Kernal config file in the /sys/conf/<SYSTEMNAME> and 
add the line:
	
controller      vga0       at eisa0     slot  ?  vector    vgaintr

This forced it to look for the isa card instead of the generic video driver.
BTW: the "slot ?" is a sort of wildcard that will let have the system search for 
the card.

-Patrick

