     HI Everyone:
     
     There is a patch for DTLOGIN that fixes this problem.  The problem 
     description follows.  I don't have the patch Id number but you can 
     request the patch from DIGITAL CSC 1-800-354-9000.
     
     Upgrading the OS to DU 4.0A apparently does not fix this problem since 
     I saw a message describing a similar problem this morning.
     
     Special thanks to 
     Alan Davis, Tim Mooney and David Notov.
     ==================================================================
     
     PROBLEM DESCRIPTION:
     
     Users attempting to login with a non-root user-id on Digital UNIX 
     V3.2D-1
     or V3.2D-2 systems with the CDE 
     Advanced Developers' Kit are refused login with the message "Sorry. 
     Maximum number of users already logged in."
     
     The same problem occurs 
     on Digital UNIX V3.2C after CSC Patch ID OSF350-004 has been 
     installed.  The afore-mentioned patch is automatically included in 
     
     Digital UNIX V3.2D-1 and V3.2D-2.
     
     OSF350-004 fixes a pair of 
     security holes in the kernel routine setsysinfo(). A side effect of 
     this change causes CDE dtlogin to reject valid logins, even if the 
     system has the proper LMF PAKs installed.
     
     
You can request a patch for dtlogin from the CSC.
     
     

