John Kohl came up with a solution, given below:

>Yep, this is a known X server bug.  I've reported it to DEC.
>
>In the meantime, to get rid of this "melting" effect, add the "-su -bs"
>flags to the X server startup line in /usr/dt/config/Xservers.con file:
>Here's what I have in that file:
>   :0   Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X -su -bs :0

I have also got response from DEC who read this list as well and there solution
is similar:

>Roberto Romani <romani@redbck.stl.dec.com>
>
>I think the problem is with backing store or save under problem with Xserver,
>I assume you are running Open 3d v4.0 as well .try modifying the Xserver config
>file i.e. /usr/dt/config/Xserver 
>
>:0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X -terminate -su -bs -I -ffbdoDMA 0 :0
>
>	-su disables save under
>	-bs disables backing store
>	-ffbdoDMA is to modify behaviour of DMA

