From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Oct 04 17:37:40 1996
From: Why not ? <gege () cal ! enst ! fr>
Date: Fri, 04 Oct 1996 17:37:40 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: digital unix 4.0 mountd returns ENOACCESS
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076340321352

	A long time ago, I asked you this question

>	I migrated to D.U. 4.0, and since then, my server refuses to serve 
>any mount request originating form one sunOS client. other clients with the
>same version of sunOS work OK. i tried to run mountd without security
>verifications and even allow non-root mount requests, but no way.
>	    mountd always returns errno 13 ENOPERM, permission denied
>	    this occurs on all file systems exported.


	The answer has been found by the digital support who looked for
the differences introduced in mountd 4.0. 
	When a client host has several adresses for the same host name,
D.U. 4.0 will refuse to honour a mount request originating from an address which
is not the first one in the list. this bug has been reported to the development
team. Meanwhile, using the 3.2D-1 mount worked fine.

