From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Oct 02 19:33:28 1996
From: Jay Sekora <jay () ccs ! neu ! edu>
Date: Wed, 02 Oct 1996 19:33:28 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] Re: RIS can't find "getname"/host names
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076340321312

Thanks to Sam Sarasin, Stuart Davidson, Pirie Hart, and Tom Reu for 
answers to my query.  Pirie Hart gave me the information I needed:

I've still got a problem booting over the net, which I will detail in 
a separate piece of mail (for filing convenience :-).

  (The following applies to DU 3.2C.  Your mileage may vary.)

[But actually it worked for 4.0A too. -j.]

  The directory "/usr/.smdb." contains the subset files.  Files with the
  ".lk" extension indicates the that the subset corresponding to the name 
  of the file, with the extension removed, is installed.  The files with
  ".ctrl", ".inv", and ".scp" should be present for all subsets which you 
  have had the option to install.
  
  The ".inv" file lists the files and directories that are included with 
  the subset.  On my system, OSFRIS350.inv includes a line for your missing 
  file "/usr/var/adm/ris/bin/getname".
  
  You should search all "*.inv" files for a reference to the appropriate
  "getname" (i.e., "grep getname *.inv").  You may find several files 
  contain "getname".  Once you have found the correct subset, reinstall it 
  using setld.

